{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And they put fire therein, and laid incense thereon.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): the sin for which Nadav and Avihu were punished is that they brought strange fire from outside, for the rule of the incense was to take fire from the altar and burn the spices with it, as it says (Leviticus 16:12) ״ולקח מלא המחתה גחלי אש מעל המזבח״. And they reasoned that the fire of the altar was needed for itself, to consume the offering; therefore they brought fire from outside, and this was a transgression on their part, for it was seen as a deficiency of faith — after all, the fire descends from heaven. And because they weakened in their hearts the power of the miracle, in the eyes of those who saw them, they were punished, for there was a certain profanation of the Name in the matter. Thus explained the Raavad, of blessed memory." "<b>By way of the Midrash:</b> they entered the Sanctuary intoxicated with wine, and therefore Scripture immediately adjoins to it: ״יין ושכר אל תשת״ and so forth. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to them: I will honor you more than you honored Me — you offered before Me impure fire; I will burn you with pure fire. How did their death come about? Two threads of fire came forth from the Holy of Holies and split into four: two entered the nostrils of this one and two entered the nostrils of that one." "<b>By way of the Kabbalah:</b> you shall understand their sin from what Scripture says, ״וישימו עליה״ — and it did not say ״וישימו עליהם,״ as it says concerning the matter of Korah (Numbers 16:18) ״ויתנו עליהם אש וישימו עליהם קטרת,״ and likewise it further mentions (there) ״ונתתם עליהם קטרת.״ For the word עליה alludes to the attribute of Judgment, and Scripture has informed us of their intention thereby. And know that the incense belongs to the attribute of Judgment, as it says (Deuteronomy 33:10) ״ישימו קטורה באפך,״ and the language of קטרת is the binding of the spirit to the attributes — Targum (Genesis 38) renders ותקשור as וקטרת. And through that binding there flows an influx from above to the attribute of Judgment, and from the attribute of Judgment comes the influx of blessing upon the one who offers the incense. And the one who offers incense to the attribute of Judgment should intend none other than the unique Name alone. Nadav and Avihu erred here in pursuing the attribute of Judgment and did not direct their intention to the unique Name but to the attribute of Judgment alone; therefore it was not ״אשה ריח ניחוח לה',״ and the attribute of Judgment itself struck them — as it is written: ״ותצא אש מלפני ה׳ ותאכל אותם.״" "<b>According to the view</b> of most of the commentators of blessed memory, they brought this incense into the innermost sanctum (לפני ולפנים), and their proof for this is the section of Acharei Mot, for there Aharon is warned not to enter the innermost area except with incense, lest he die in the manner that his sons died. And this is the view of Rashi and of the sage Rabbi Avraham ibn Ezra, of blessed memory." "<b>But</b> the view of the Ramban, of blessed memory, is that they did not enter the innermost sanctum but rather were in the Tent of Meeting. And so he wrote at the beginning of the section of Acharei Mot: how could it enter their minds to come today to the place where their own father never entered, and why would they bring their incense there, to the innermost area, more than he did? For Aharon never burned incense on the inner altar except in the Tent of Meeting, as it is written ״ויבא משה ואהרן אל אהל מועד,״ and this entry was to teach him the procedure of the incense."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:24:33.859683754Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}